# science-article-gnn

GNN on RelBench entity tasks, trained and evaluated on original and masked data.

## Setup (Google Colab)

```
!git clone https://github.com/Nok1sh/science-article-gnn.git
%cd science-article-gnn
!python install.py
```

## Usage

```python
from relgnn import load_data, masks, train

original = load_data("rel-f1", "driver-position")
masked = load_data("rel-f1", "driver-position", mask=masks.noise(0.1))

model = train(original, epochs=25)
model.evaluate(original)   # {"val": {"nmae": ...}, "test": {"nmae": ...}}
model.evaluate(masked)     # the same model on masked data

model.save("checkpoints/f1.pt")
```

Sweep over masks:

```python
rows = []
for mask in [None, masks.noise(0.1), masks.noise(0.5), masks.shuffle(0.5)]:
    data = load_data("rel-f1", "driver-position", mask=mask)
    model = train(data, epochs=25, verbose=False)
    rows.append({"trained_on": data.name, **model.evaluate(original)["test"]})
```

## Masks

Built in: `masks.noise(strength)`, `masks.shuffle(fraction)`, `masks.from_dir(path)`.

Own mask: a function editing the database in place, wrapped in `Mask`:

```python
from relgnn import Mask

def drop_names(db, col_to_stype_dict, rng):
    db.table_dict["drivers"].df["surname"] = "unknown"

data = load_data("rel-f1", "driver-position", mask=Mask("drop_names", drop_names))
```

Masks may change feature columns only: rows, primary keys and foreign keys must stay
as they are (checked on load). See `relgnn/masks.py`.

| Module | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `relgnn/data.py` | `load_data`, `RelData` |
| `relgnn/training.py` | `train`, `TrainConfig`, `TrainedModel` (`evaluate`, `predict`, `save`, `load`) |
| `relgnn/masks.py` | `Mask`, built-in masks, `export_tables`, structure checks |
| `relgnn/graph.py` | database → heterogeneous graph |
| `relgnn/model.py` | the GNN (from RelBench examples) |
